{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id701590776"}, "name":{"label":"iceice15"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-01-05T05:16:11-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"2"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.86.8"}, "id":{"label":"12147818960"}, "title":{"label":"Only download if you’ll get the subscription."}, "content":{"label":"The concept of this app is great honestly but only if you’re willing to pay. I downloaded it because I saw plenty of good reviews and I was surprised when I downloaded the app and saw that almost every feature is behind a paywall. A few features I can understand you’d prefer to keep them for subscribers, but what do you mean I can’t add a missed drink from the day before unless I pay £16.99 a year or a one time £19.99 for lifetime? I have a music tracking app that I paid a one time lifetime subscription for only £8.99, but I’m supposed to believe an app where I have to MANUALLY track my water intake is worth more than 50% of that? I wouldn’t be this annoyed if at least the ‘add missed drink’ feature was free, because come on… what sense does it make for it to not be free?? \n\nOther than that I think it’s a good idea of an app and the free version is very simple if all you want is a tracking app. Just make sure you track all your intake before midnight cause this app will not let you add anything else as soon as it’s 12:01am.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=1454778585&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
